    description: "Found by the 2026-10-05 docstring staleness audit and reproduced on the shipped CLI: for 'enum Kind implements Shape' no implements edge exists, while 'record Circle(...) implements Shape' (inheritance-linker) and 'class Sq implements Shape' (java) both have one. Consequence: enum method dispatch through the interface is invisible to inherited_calls and type_hierarchy. java.py's module docstring now states the gap."  # 86a6
    fields:  # 86a6
      statement: "Every declared supertype relation in a supported language yields an extends/implements edge."  # 86a6
      root_cause: "java.py emits extends/implements edges only inside 'if node.type == \"class_declaration\"' (~L2547). Records and interfaces get edges via meta base_classes and the core inheritance linker; enums carry nothing that linker reads."  # 86a6
